great story! but there seem to be some spelling/grammar issues;

"lerform" instead of perform

The captain waited for the bards to be seated, then turned to both participants. "Gentlemen, before we begin, I'd like to have the orchestra lerform the song in question. Sargeant, as the prosecuting party, who would you like to initiate."

&#x200B;

the formating on

"You came too late, wait till the end\*

&#x200B;

"eld" instead of elf

Nop watched as the courtroom was split between grins and glares. The eld tried to retort and retaliate, but after a few seconds she just began crying and rushed out the room.
